- Output Markdown only. No preamble. Start with a short summary paragraph.
- Do not write a title of your own: no line starting with "#". The document already carries its title, and a second one in the body is a duplicate.
- Call out what a PEER TEAM needs to know: a changed interface, a new capability, a deprecation, a behaviour change someone else could be affected by, a shared dependency. A peer team is anyone who depends on this project and does not own it. "What shipped" is not the same question as "what changes for me", and a report that only answers the first is a status list, not an update.

